From: Alejandro Corbellini <acorbellini@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 03 Mar 2026 11:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: rk817-battery: fast-forward dsoc on resume
 after charging

When the device is suspended while charging, the hardware coulomb
counter continues accumulating charge but the displayed SOC (dsoc)
is frozen. On resume, rsoc (real SOC from hardware) can be much
higher than dsoc, but the smooth algorithm only increments dsoc by
small amounts per cycle, taking many minutes of wake time to catch
up.

Fix this by jumping dsoc directly to rsoc on resume when the device
was charging during sleep and rsoc exceeds dsoc. This gives the
user an immediately accurate battery percentage after opening the
lid.

Signed-off-by: Alejandro Corbellini <acorbellini@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/rk817_battery.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_battery.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_battery.c
@@ -3375,6 +3375,17 @@
 			battery->sleep_dischrg_sec = 0;
 	}
 
+	/* If charged during sleep, fast-forward dsoc to match rsoc.
+	 * The smooth algorithm would eventually catch up, but it
+	 * takes many minutes of wake time. Jump immediately so the
+	 * user sees the correct percentage on resume.
+	 */
+	if (battery->sleep_chrg_online && battery->rsoc > battery->dsoc) {
+		BAT_INFO("resume: chrg dsoc jump %d -> %d\n",
+			 battery->dsoc, battery->rsoc);
+		battery->dsoc = battery->rsoc;
+	}
+
 	rk817_bat_save_data(battery);
 
 	/* charge/lowpower lock: for battery work to update dsoc and rsoc */
